@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title G1 · One publication boundary, one shared contract
top to bottom direction
$producer(producers, "Human authors · Analysers · Third-party tools\nProducers")
$validator(validation, "Publication validation\nCompleteness and consistency")
$package(contract, "Authoritative AIL package\nDeclared API surface and its contract")
$catalogue(catalogue, "Profile and ABI catalogue entries\nSelected by identifier, version and digest")
$consumer(consumers, "Binding generators · Documentation renderers · LLM tooling\nConsumers")
producers --> validation : submit under the same rules
validation --> contract : publish only when complete and consistent
contract -right-> catalogue : pins
contract --> consumers : supplies the same contract
note left of validation
  Does not prove that a binary
  honours the assertions.
end note
legend bottom
  Proposed roles, not running tools. Non-normative: L2–L3, C8, A1, A5.
  Shapes: rectangle = producer; hexagon = validator; folder = package;
  cylinder = catalogue; component = consumer.
  Labelled arrows show publication, dependency or consumption, not runtime calls.
endlegend
@enduml
